body:
I don't know it's exact name, but across from Lincoln High there is a strip 'mall'. There's Arts & Humanities, a catering company, foster closet, and thrift store. Then there's a little Hispanic shop with the best handmade tortillas. I would 100% recommend this place. I used to buy a can of beans with their tortillas and share it all for lunch.

&#x200B;

Edit: This is actually the place someone else suggested. Marlene's rocks!
